# Learn more https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files
.env
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# generated native folders — EAS regenerates these from app.json on every build
# (Continuous Native Generation). Do not commit them; doing so makes the native
# project the source of truth and silently overrides app.json config.
/ios
/android
supabase/.temp/

# The same rule, one level down: @bacons/apple-targets writes these into each
# targets/<name>/ folder from that target's expo-target.config.js on every
# prebuild. Committing them doesn't make them the source of truth — it just
# means nothing ever re-derives them, so they go stale and ship.
#
# They did. The watch target carried a committed $accent of rgb(0,.545,.545),
# a teal, long after the config declared #34C77B, and a 1024 app icon that was
# still the old chevron rather than the ichthys. Both shipped. They also
# collided with every pull, because a local prebuild rewrites them.
#
# Info.plist is the exception and stays tracked: targets/watch/Info.plist is
# hand-edited (it registers UIAppFonts for the app's faces), and the plugin
# only writes that file when it is absent — so an ignored one would come back
# generated, without the fonts. The targets that do not hand-edit theirs are
# listed individually below rather than with a wildcard, so adding a target
# has to make this choice deliberately.
targets/*/Assets.xcassets/
targets/*/generated.entitlements
targets/widget/Info.plist
targets/watch-widget/Info.plist
